          "UI (User Interface) and UX (User Experience) design are two interrelated disciplines that shape how users interact with digital products. UX focuses on the overall experience — how intuitive and satisfying a product is to use. UI focuses on the visual and interactive elements — buttons, typography, colour, spacing. Great products need both: an excellent UX with poor UI feels rough and untrustworthy, while beautiful UI with poor UX frustrates users despite its good looks.\n\nInvesting in professional UI/UX design directly impacts business outcomes. Studies consistently show that every £1 invested in UX returns £100 in value. Products with strong UX design see higher user adoption, lower churn, fewer support tickets, and better Net Promoter Scores. For digital businesses in competitive markets like Indonesia and Singapore, design quality is a genuine differentiator.",
