        id: "common-mistakes",
        heading: "Common Brand Identity Mistakes to Avoid",
        content:
          "The most common mistake is confusing a logo with a brand identity. A logo is one element of a system — without accompanying colours, typography, and guidelines, even a great logo will be applied inconsistently and lose its impact. The second mistake is designing for founders rather than customers — choosing elements that reflect personal taste rather than what resonates with the target audience.\n\nInconsistency is the brand killer most businesses underestimate. Using five different shades of your 'blue' across different materials, mixing font weights arbitrarily, or applying the logo at different sizes without a grid — these details erode the sense of professionalism and quality that strong branding is supposed to convey. Brand guidelines exist precisely to prevent this entropy.",
