        content:
          "A landing page experiment — sometimes called a 'smoke test' — lets you measure demand signal at scale before building. Build a landing page that describes the product as if it exists (honest about its pre-launch status), drive targeted traffic to it, and measure how many visitors take a high-intent action: joining a waitlist, requesting early access, or clicking a 'Sign Up' button that leads to a 'Coming Soon' message.\n\nThe goal isn't to deceive — it's to measure interest with real-world behaviour rather than survey responses. Traffic can come from targeted LinkedIn ads, Reddit posts in relevant communities, cold outreach, or your own network. A conversion rate above 10-15% on a focused audience is a strong signal. Below 5% warrants a rethink of either the positioning or the problem you're solving.",
